```javascript
mongodb_list_collections()
```

2. Then, get the databases to work with:
```javascript
mongodb_list_databases()
```

3. For each game type you're interested in, run these queries:
- Get the collection indexes and schema:
```javascript
mongodb_collection_indexes(collection_name)
mongodb_collection_schema(collection_name)
```
- List all records for that month (December 2023):
```javascript
mongodb_find(
    collection_name,
    database_name,
    {
        "date": { "$gte": new Date("2023-12-01") },
        "date": { "$lte": new Date("2023-12-31") }
    }
)
```
- Sort the records by quantity (descending) and get the closest to end of month:
```javascript
mongodb_find(
    collection_name,
    database_name,
    {
        "date": { "$gte": new Date("2023-12-01") },
        "date": { "$lte": new Date("2023-12-31") }
    },
    {
        "sort": { "quantity": -1 }
    }
)
```

4. Once you have the records, analyze which game type has the highest quantity:
```javascript
mongodb_find(
    collection_name,
    database_name,
    {
        "date": { "$gte": new Date("2023-12-01") },
        "date": { "$lte": new Date("2023-12-31") }
    },
    {
